<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 51 0 R
/E (With AI already widely used in schools and homes, we take a human-centred and pragmatic approach to help decision-makers act while longitudinal evidence on its learning impacts develops. We believe that AI should support and not replace the relational, ethical, and motivational roles of teachers, caregivers, and peers.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
111 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 51 0 R
/E (Drawing on a structured review of global evidence and consultations with government officials, NGOs, and experts in France, Canada, Egypt and Qatar, the report is written for governments, schools, regulators and funders, and sets out the conditions under which EdTech and AI providers can contribute positively to AI literacy \(Table 1 and Box 10\).)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
